# Architecture

The diagram below shows what the {{ dg.productName }} contains, which pieces are created per connection versus shared globally, and how a call flows from the user application down to the database.

```mermaid
flowchart TB
  app["User Application"]

  subgraph entry["Entry points"]
    direction LR
{% for ep in dg.diagram.entryPoints %}
    ep{{ loop.index }}["{{ ep }}"]
{% endfor %}
  end

  subgraph conn["{{ dg.diagram.wrapperNode }} — one per {{ dg.connectionShort }}"]
    direction TB
    pm["{{ dg.pluginManagerTitle }}"]
    plugins["Loaded plugins<br/>(subscribed to {{ dg.methodTerm }})"]
    terminus["{{ dg.diagram.terminusPlugin }}<br/>(pipeline terminus)"]
    subgraph perconn["Per-connection services"]
      direction LR
{% for svc in dg.services %}{% if not svc.global and svc.short != "Plugin Manager" %}
{% if svc.short == dg.diagram.hostListProviderOwner %}
      subgraph pc{{ loop.index }}["{{ svc.short }}"]
        hlp["Host List Provider"]
      end
{% else %}
      pc{{ loop.index }}["{{ svc.short }}"]
{% endif %}
{% endif %}{% endfor %}
    end
  end

  subgraph shared["Shared / global services (reused across connections)"]
    direction LR
{% for svc in dg.services %}{% if svc.global %}
{% if svc.short == "Monitor Service" %}
      subgraph g{{ loop.index }}["Monitor Service"]
        mon["Background monitors<br/>(e.g. topology, blue/green)"]
      end
{% else %}
      g{{ loop.index }}["{{ svc.short }}"]
{% endif %}
{% endif %}{% endfor %}
  end

  db[("Database / Aurora cluster")]

  app --> entry
{% for ep in dg.diagram.entryPoints %}
  ep{{ loop.index }} --> pm
{% endfor %}
  pm --> plugins
  plugins --> perconn

  %% Two kinds of code open a connection to the database:
  %% (1) the terminus plugin opens the connection your application uses,
  plugins --> terminus
  terminus -->|"opens the application connection"| db
  %% (2) background monitors each use their OWN separate connection.
  mon -->|"separate connection(s): topology / blue-green status"| db
```

The {{ dg.productName }} contains {{ dg.componentCount }} main components:

{{ dg.architectureComponents.strip() }}

The {{ dg.pluginManagerShort }} handles all the loaded or registered plugins and sends the {{ dg.methodTermSingular }} to be executed by all plugins [**subscribed**](./loadable-plugins#subscribed-methods) to that method.

During execution, plugins may utilize the [service container](./service-container) to help their execution by retrieving or updating:

- the current connection
- the hosts information
- topology of the database

:::note

- Each {{ dg.connectionObject }} has its own instances of:
  - plugin manager
  - service container
  - loaded plugin classes
- Multiple {{ dg.connectionObject }}s opened to the same database server will have separate sets of instances mentioned above.
- The shared storage, monitor, and event-publisher services (and the host list provider) are reused across connections to the same database.

:::
